 "text": "Hi, how are you holding up? Sorry about the pads. A thin layer of paper between them helps without going the open box route. Not really, left hand uses impact more than the pad, so a full size keyboard without any track pad at all is the biggest improvement. Laptop one is the easiest to handle left handed. Look for ones with the keys far apart, like this. It makes writing fast without the pad annoyingly getting in the way.",
